// @check
// @error-at 6:11 `type` is a keyword and can't name a parameter — rename it
// A keyword in a binding position is ONE error, at the declaration (D3069, plumb PL-071). The
// parser reads the keyword as the name for recovery only, so the uses below — a condition, an
// operand, a statement that leads with the name — report nothing further. Whether a keyword may
// name a binding is a language decision; this file pins the diagnostic, not a new spelling.
function f(type: i64) { if type == 0 { return -1 }; type + 1 }
